  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the leatherback turtle (dermochelys coriacea) in the Mexican Pacific.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring and Protection of the Nesting Population: to estimate the nesting population size per year of the leatherback turtle along the Mexican Pacific, to protect at least 90% of the total number of clutches laid in the index beaches, having at least 60% of hatching success, to compile information from the protection activities on secondary beaches and provide training and technical assistance, To evaluate the environmental conditions which affect the hatching success at the nesting beaches.</narrative>
  </description>
